// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR:
//
// C backend twin of conformance/arrays/out_of_bounds.astra (audit finding S11).
// The generated code wrote `a[5]` straight through `AstraArray.elems`, so this
// program read and wrote outside the heap buffer: the read printed garbage with
// exit 0 and `a[5] = 99` was ASan-confirmed memory corruption. Indexing now goes
// through astra_array_get/astra_array_set, which report the same bounds error as
// the VM. The runner requires exit 1 with a "runtime error" line, so a crash
// (also non-zero) cannot pass this test.
fn main() {
    let a = [1, 2, 3]
    print(a[5])
}
